{"seq":1,"at":"2026-09-17","kind":"imported","target":{"type":"article","id":"a1152"},"reason":"Article of the Quiztopia bank (written for card c096): researched and transcribed in September 2026, converted to the quiz platform on 2026-10-20.","by":"Quiztopia import","ref":"quiz-archive/transcripts/quiztopia/c096.json"},
{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a1152"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge technology/inventions","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/technology__inventions.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",928],["+","Some names became trademarks so completely that they stand for the machine itself. Frank Zamboni, the son of Italian immigrants, ran an ice rink in Paramount, California, where resurfacing the ice by hand – scraping, washing and flooding it – took five workers 90 minutes. In 1947 he built a vehicle that did all of it in one pass, and in 1949 he applied for a patent on it: shaving the surface, collecting the shavings and laying down a thin film of warm water that freezes smooth. The figure skater Sonja Henie ordered two for her touring show, and ice hockey arenas followed. His surname was registered as a trademark, and today anyone sitting on a Zamboni is smoothing the ice of a rink, usually between periods of a hockey game.\n\n"],["=",109],["+","\n| the Zamboni ice resurfacer | Frank Zamboni | 1947/1949 |"]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",906],["+","Manche Namen wurden so vollständig zur Marke, dass sie für die Maschine selbst stehen. Frank Zamboni, Sohn italienischer Einwanderer, betrieb in Paramount, Kalifornien, eine Eisbahn, auf der das Aufbereiten des Eises von Hand – Abschaben, Waschen und Fluten – fünf Arbeiter 90 Minuten kostete. 1947 baute er ein Fahrzeug, das alles in einem Durchgang erledigte, und 1949 meldete er es zum Patent an: Es hobelte die Oberfläche ab, sammelte die Späne ein und legte einen dünnen Film warmen Wassers auf, der glatt gefriert. Die Eiskunstläuferin Sonja Henie bestellte zwei für ihre Tournee-Show, und die Eishockeyhallen folgten. Sein Nachname wurde als Marke eingetragen, und wer heute auf einer Zamboni sitzt, glättet das Eis einer Eisbahn, meist in den Drittelpausen eines Eishockeyspiels.\n\n"],["=",103],["+","\n| die Zamboni-Eismaschine | Frank Zamboni | 1947/1949 |"]]}]},
